<!-- MINDONE 15.09: hide the gesture "pill" at the bottom of the screen (product decision).

     The white bar is drawn by SystemUI's NavigationHandle
     (packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/navigationbar/gestural/NavigationHandle.java),
     which paints a rounded rect in navigation_bar_home_handle_light_color or
     ..._dark_color depending on the background. Making both fully transparent removes the
     bar and NOTHING else: the view still exists, still has its size, and every gesture
     region, inset and animation is untouched. That is deliberate - this is the one way to
     remove it that cannot break navigation.

     🔴 What does NOT work, checked rather than assumed: LineageSettings.NAVIGATION_BAR_HINT
     exists as a constant but nothing in this tree reads it - grep over frameworks/base,
     lineage-sdk, LineageParts and vendor/lineage finds only its declaration in
     LineageSettings.java. Setting it has no effect at all.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="navigation_bar_home_handle_light_color">#00000000</color>
    <color name="navigation_bar_home_handle_dark_color">#00000000</color>
</resources>
